Your final score in NetHack is comprised of four (IIRC) components:
killing monsters, collecting treasure, exploring the dungeon, and
oddball things like oiling squeaky boards. I think it would be neat if
the extended logfile recorded each of those values.

A while back I tried to write a patch for a new scoring algorithm since
people seem to think the NetHack scoring system is broken, but nobody
liked the system I devised. Perhaps with the breakdown of scores from
10000 tournament games next year I could do some sort of statistical
analysis and come up with a better scheme.



